---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy and Local Processing"
  description="What stays on your device, how saved settings work and what ordinary website requests involve."
  noindex
  activeNav="/about/"
>
  <section class="legal-hero legal-shell">
    <p class="eyebrow">SELLER OPERATIONS LAB</p><h1>
      Privacy and local processing
    </h1>
  </section>
  <section class="legal-content legal-shell">
    <p>Updated October 21, 2026.</p>
    <h2>Selected files</h2><p>
      Image Prep, Image QA and the format-comparison tool process selected files
      in your browser. They do not upload them to Seller Operations Lab or store
      them in a server-side image library. There is no account or cloud
      synchronization.
    </p>
    <h2>Saved settings</h2><p>
      Saving is optional. Image settings and filename preferences may be stored
      in this browser's local storage. Photos and source image bytes are not
      stored there. Use “Forget saved settings” to remove the saved recipe.
    </p>
    <h2>Ordinary website requests</h2><p>
      Loading the site involves network requests. Cloudflare, our hosting
      provider, may process connection and security information such as IP
      addresses, requested URLs and request times. Local image processing does
      not mean every website visit is anonymous. See <a
        href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer">Cloudflare's privacy policy</a
      >.
    </p>
    <h2>Hosting performance measurement</h2><p>
      The deployed site loads a Cloudflare Web Analytics performance beacon,
      which Cloudflare can inject at the hosting layer even though it is not in
      this repository's page scripts. It reports page-view and
      loading-performance information to Cloudflare. This is separate from
      processing your selected image files; the image tools do not send those
      files to the analytics service.
    </p><p>
      Cloudflare documents the beacon's collection and reporting behavior in its <a
        href="https://developers.cloudflare.com/web-analytics/data-metrics/data-origin-and-collection/"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer">Web Analytics data collection documentation</a
      >. Ordinary hosting and security requests are described above; do not
      interpret local image processing as a claim that the site makes no
      external requests.
    </p>
    <h2>Advertising</h2><p>
      This release does not run advertising scripts. If advertising or
      additional analytics is enabled later, this policy and any applicable
      consent controls must be reviewed and updated before those scripts run.
    </p>
    <h2>External links and contact</h2><p>
      Marketplace documentation and GitHub open services with their own privacy
      practices. GitHub issue reports are public; do not post images, personal
      details or confidential business information. <a href="/contact/"
        >Contact and corrections</a
      >.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
